      "source": [
        "import nltk\n",
        "from nltk.corpus import stopwords\n",
        "from nltk.stem import WordNetLemmatizer\n",
        "import re\n",
        "\n",
        "try:\n",
        "    stopwords.words('english')\n",
        "except LookupError:\n",
        "    nltk.download('stopwords')\n",
        "    print(\"NLTK 'stopwords' downloaded.\")\n",
        "\n",
        "try:\n",
        "    nltk.data.find('corpora/wordnet')\n",
        "except LookupError:\n",
        "    nltk.download('wordnet')\n",
        "    print(\"NLTK 'wordnet' downloaded.\")\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "lemmatizer = WordNetLemmatizer()\n",
        "stop_words = set(stopwords.words('english'))\n",
        "\n",
        "def preprocess_text(text):\n",
        "    text = str(text).lower()\n",
        "    text = re.sub(r'[^a-z\\s]', '', text)\n",
        "    words = text.split()\n",
        "    # Lemmatize and remove stopwords\n",
        "    words = [lemmatizer.lemmatize(word) for word in words if word not in stop_words and len(word) > 2]\n",
        "    return ' '.join(words)\n",
        "\n",
        "df['processed_headline'] = df['headline'].apply(preprocess_text)\n",
        "display(df[['headline', 'processed_headline']].head())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "bcc3fd67"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Feature Extraction with TF-IDF\n",
        "\n",
        "Now that the text is preprocessed, we'll convert it into a numerical format using TF-IDF (Term Frequency-Inverse Document Frequency). TF-IDF reflects how important a word is to a document in a collection or corpus. Words that are common in many documents will have lower TF-IDF scores, while unique and important words will have higher scores. This helps in focusing on relevant terms for topic modeling."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "b0907840",
        "outputId": "ed098cb4-370d-4416-f538-96a50f0722ad"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "TF-IDF Matrix Shape: (2658, 1678)\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "from sklearn.feature_extraction.text import TfidfVectorizer\n",
        "\n",
        "# Initialize TF-IDF Vectorizer\n",
        "tfidf_vectorizer = TfidfVectorizer(max_df=0.95, min_df=2, stop_words='english')\n",
        "\n",
        "# Fit and transform the processed headlines\n",
        "tfidf_matrix = tfidf_vectorizer.fit_transform(df['processed_headline'])\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"TF-IDF Matrix Shape: {tfidf_matrix.shape}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "acbe05b1"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Topic Modeling with Latent Dirichlet Allocation (LDA)\n",
        "\n",
        "Latent Dirichlet Allocation (LDA) is a generative statistical model that allows sets of observations to be explained by unobserved groups that explain why some parts of the data are similar. In the context of text, this means it can uncover abstract \"topics\" that occur in a collection of documents.\n",
        "\n",
        "We will apply LDA to the TF-IDF matrix to identify the main topics present in the headlines. The number of topics (`n_components`) is a hyperparameter that often requires experimentation to find the optimal value."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "552094fb",
        "outputId": "cb624913-5709-4b63-a2fb-8c37f7aa4528"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "LDA Output Shape: (2658, 5)\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "from sklearn.decomposition import LatentDirichletAllocation\n",
        "\n",
        "# Number of topics to extract\n",
        "num_topics = 5 # This can be adjusted based on the dataset and desired granularity\n",
        "\n",
        "# Initialize LDA model\n",
        "lda_model = LatentDirichletAllocation(n_components=num_topics, random_state=42)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Fit LDA model to the TF-IDF matrix\n",
        "lda_output = lda_model.fit_transform(tfidf_matrix)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"LDA Output Shape: {lda_output.shape}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "3cc0c88a"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Displaying Top Keywords for Each Topic\n",
        "\n",
        "To understand what each topic represents, we can examine the top words (keywords) that contribute most to each topic. These keywords help in interpreting the thematic content of each identified topic."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "a48bb238",
        "outputId": "cc071125-bae1-4b51-85a5-3aa5f75ff60b"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "Topic 1:\n",
            "biggest mover yesterday estimate beat sale eps miss new earnings\n",
            "Topic 2:\n",
            "benzingas etf downgrade upgrade april change volume chatter partner ceo\n",
            "Topic 3:\n",
            "week hit stock low thursday high eps yoy sale report\n",
            "Topic 4:\n",
            "target price maintains raise lower buy neutral morgan announces american\n",
            "Topic 5:\n",
            "session moving stock premarket share higher trading company midday market\n",
            "\n",
            "\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "feature_names = tfidf_vectorizer.get_feature_names_out()\n",
        "\n",
        "def display_topics(model, feature_names, num_top_words):\n",
        "    for topic_idx, topic in enumerate(model.components_):\n",
        "        print(f\"Topic {topic_idx + 1}:\")\n",
        "        print(\" \".join([feature_names[i]\n",
        "                        for i in topic.argsort()[:-num_top_words - 1:-1]]))\n",
        "    print(\"\\n\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Display top 10 words for each topic\n",
        "display_topics(lda_model, feature_names, 10)"
      ]
    },
